Answer: Each entity can be handled by a separate for loop. If a pattern has two entities, two loops are used. If a pattern has three entities, three loops are used. For example, a pattern containing: Number of rows Number of stars in each row can be handled using:

```java
for (int j = 1; j <= rows; j++) {
for (int i = 1; i <= stars; i++) {
System.out.print("*");
}
System.out.println();
}
```

Here, the outer loop handles the rows and the inner loop handles the stars.

Answer: After the loop prints all five stars, use System.out.println() without any value.

```java
for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
System.out.print("*");
}
System.out.println();
```

println() with no argument does not print additional content. It only moves the cursor to the next line.

