Here: j = 5 → inner loop runs 5 times j = 4 → inner loop runs 4 times j = 3 → inner loop runs 3 times j = 2 → inner loop runs 2 times j = 1 → inner loop runs 1 time This is another valid perspective for the same output.

Answer: Consider: 5 5 5 5 5 4 4 4 4 3 3 3 2 2 1 The row values are decreasing: 5 4 3 2 1 The number of repetitions also decreases: 5 repetitions 4 repetitions 3 repetitions 2 repetitions 1 repetition The row value is what must be printed. A suitable structure is:

```java
for (int j = 5; j >= 1; j--) {
for (int i = 1; i <= j; i++) {
System.out.print(j + " ");
}
System.out.println();
}
```

The outer loop controls the decreasing row value, while the inner loop controls how many times that value is printed.

